{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfjpbdrzQGvj5tbN2qi4X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate `gamblers_second_order_person_lapse` and it passes the self-check. That check is only a short smoke fit, though: it says nothing about convergence, the 30-minute limit or novelty, and the 30-minute limit is a real risk.\n\n**What I changed:** I refined the incumbent `gamblers_run_second_order_side_habit` with one change. Each person now has their own lapse rate. On that share of trials they don't judge the pair at all and pick Left or Right at random:\n\n`p_left = (1 − λᵢ)·sigmoid(evidence + sideᵢ) + λᵢ/2`\n\nThe lapse rates come from a population (400 slots), with a prior that keeps most people's rate low. Everything else is the incumbent's code, unchanged.\n\n**Why:** The critique's strongest finding is that people differ more than the model allows in how often they agree with the majority (z = 3.17, q = 0.064, just short of surviving the FDR correction). A lapse limits how often a person can agree with the majority even on clear-cut pairs. A lower sensitivity mostly flattens near-ties instead, so the two make different predictions. Pulling every choice towards 50/50 also plausibly helps with the weaker finding that people prefer more switches in short pairs less often than predicted.\n\n**Check result:** it printed `OK`. On that short fit the ELPD-LOO was −3601.7, against the incumbent's −3611.7. That number comes from 100 draws on one chain, so it isn't a fair comparison.\n\n**Risks:**\n- **Speed:** the check took about 20 minutes for 200 iterations on one chain. If admission's full fit runs at a similar pace, it may hit the 30-minute limit and be rejected as too slow. I don't know how long the incumbent itself takes to fit.\n- **Convergence:** each person's lapse rate may trade off against their sensitivity, which could hurt convergence.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2213,"cache_read_input_tokens":81759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2213,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"645804a3-10bd-4216-9818-b1ab419bbc0e","uuid":"5835fdeb-33a8-4f37-aa14-1d6f2f4611c1","timestamp":"2026-10-05T21:44:44.279Z","request_id":"req_011CfjpbcepfwGxvyAPsqHQK"}
